# Options the image build sets over the source's configuration, merged after the
# fragments and checked the same way. CONFIG_LOCALVERSION is cleared by the build itself
# (the release is set on the make command line).
#
# No build-time signing key. With the default key path, every build generates a new
# random key, compiles its certificate into the kernel and signs every module with it,
# so no two builds give the same kernel or modules. Module signature checking itself
# stays as the source configures it (the lockdown LSM selects it); it doesn't enforce
# signatures (CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE off, lockdown forced to none), so unsigned modules
# load, with the kernel marked tainted.
# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_ALL is not set
CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_KEY=""
